   "mechanism": "PNPLA3 encodes a protein that localizes to the membrane of lipid droplets in hepatocytes, where it normally exerts triglyceride lipase and transacylase activities to regulate lipid remodeling. Genetic variants in PNPLA3, such as the I148M substitution, disrupt normal triglyceride metabolism. This impaired ability to process triglycerides results in pathological intrahepatic lipid accumulation, directly promoting metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease. Multiple large genome-wide association studies firmly establish this genetic linkage.",
