   "hypothesis_id": "hypothesis_2",
   "mechanism": "APOE, APOA5, and LIPC participate in an interacting protein network that coordinates plasma lipoprotein assembly, remodeling, and clearance. APOA5 stimulates hepatic triglyceride hydrolysis via LIPC, whilst APOE mediates the uptake of VLDL, chylomicron remnants, and intermediate-density lipoproteins by hepatocytes. Dysfunction within this complex impairs normal lipid efflux and systemic triglyceride homeostasis. This disruption forces maladaptive lipid retention in the liver, leading to steatotic liver disease, a mechanism corroborated by robust genetic associations mapping each gene to the disease.",
