   "hypothesis_id": "hypothesis_3",
   "mechanism": "CMIP (c-Maf-inducing protein) undergoes epigenetic regulation by Dnmt1 and Tet2 which modulates its methylation status. These changes in CMIP dynamically govern the Gbp2-PPARγ-CD36 axis, a signaling cascade that strongly promotes lipid uptake and accumulation in the liver. Pathological activation of this axis due to aberrant CMIP levels drives the development of hepatic steatosis, linking CMIP genetic variations such as rs2925979 directly to non-alcoholic fatty liver disease.",
